From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Nap after 20 ms on the BCM4388

With power save on and the 2000 ms sleep return, the BCM4388 in the
M4 MacBook Pro stays awake two seconds after each frame. Any steady
background traffic keeps it awake almost all the time. A 20 ms return
cut the quiet Wi-Fi rail from 477 mW to 114 mW on that machine. macOS
idles at 118 mW on the same hardware. Average ping went from 6.6 ms
to 12.4 ms.

Use 20 ms as the BCM4388 default when nobody set a timeout.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index fdd00e0820..1cd177e2a6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@
 #define BRCMF_ND_INFO_TIMEOUT		msecs_to_jiffies(2000)
 
 #define BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS		2000
+#define BRCMF_PS_4388_TIMEOUT_MS	20
 
 #define BRCMF_LPAS_UNICAST_FILTER_ID	100
 #define BRCMF_LPAS_MAGIC_FILTER_ID	101
@@ -3484,6 +3485,8 @@ brcmf_cfg80211_dump_station(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 static u32 brcmf_ps_default_timeout(struct brcmf_pub *drvr)
 {
 	switch (drvr->bus_if->chip) {
+	case BRCM_CC_4388_CHIP_ID:
+		return BRCMF_PS_4388_TIMEOUT_MS;
 	default:
 		return BRCMF_PS_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS;
 	}
